Test rg78: flexo packs codes, not source characters
// Each word is derived by hand from the shared table, Tools/UtilLibs/flexoConversion.c:
// a 61, b 62, c 63, / 21, space 00, O 46, k 42; an upper-case letter is its
// lower-case code after upper shift 74, lower shift is 72; backslash is shifted
// 20, ? shifted 21; \n 77, \B 34, \R 35. A word holds the first three codes,
// padded with space codes; no shift code is added after the last character.
100/
// 77, padded
    flexo \n
// a, 77, b: 617762
    flexo a\nb
// upper shift, backslash: 742000; the ; ends the operand
    flexo \\;
// a, upper shift, backslash: 617420
    flexo a\\;
// upper shift, backslash, lower shift; a not kept: 742072
    flexo \\a
// a, b, upper shift; backslash not kept: 616274
    flexo ab\\;
// upper shift, backslash, lower shift: 742072
    flexo \\ab
// a, upper shift, backslash: 617420
    flexo a\\b
// upper shift, A: 746100
    flexo A
// upper shift, A, lower shift: 746172
    flexo Ab
// a, upper shift, B: 617462
    flexo aB
// upper shift, O, lower shift: 744672
    flexo Ok?
// a, b, c: 616263
    flexo abc
// a comment after a line-end backslash keeps the preprocessor from joining the next line: 742000
    flexo \\ // the manual's form
// the same: 616274
    flexo ab\\ // the manual's form
// black, red, carriage return: 343577
    flexo \B\R\n
// a, then the comment: 610000
    flexo a // a comment after one character
// a, space, b: 610062
    flexo a b
// a, slash, b: 612162
    flexo a/b
// a, b, c; d not kept: 616263
    flexo abcd
stop
